p='site/index.html';s=open(p).read();k='window.PATCH_NOTES = [\n';assert k in s
s=s.replace(k,k+"{v:'v1.0.115',d:'The loading screen now shows the gold Glencraft logo in the new font straight away, matching the menu, instead of the old blue glow, and it follows your UI colour choice from the start.'},\n"+"{v:'v1.0.114',d:'SPACE: the rocket now flies through the Firmament (y 300) and the atmosphere, with the Highlands map shrinking below, into real space from y 1000 - zero gravity, no drag, perpetual drift. Deep space is 24000 x 24000 with the whole solar system as blocky voxel planets: Sun, Mercury, Venus, Earth, Moon, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn and its ring, Uranus, Neptune and Pluto. TARGET picks a planet and the rocket steers for it, with WARP speed out in the empty bits. The Moon is a real block world (grey regolith, craters, low gravity) and it is the same moon you see in the night sky. Mars is a 288 x 288 block world of red sand, rock, mesas, craters and a canyon with Mars gravity. Land, build, and everything you place is saved. EXIT in deep space for a zero-g space walk - a jetpack thrusts you in any direction. The rocket camera now looks along the flight path and tilts with the rocket. Planet colours come from Solar System animation by Samer_Arab_S5 (CC-BY-4.0).'},\n"+"{v:'v1.0.113', d:'2026-11-02', notes:['Agartha fix: the cave hole is now cut into the ice wall at the point nearest Blackstone Castle - the castle is only the landmark and nothing joins the two - and the tunnel runs straight out of the map for 2000 blocks to Agartha outside the map','The flying saucer now lives in Agartha and never despawns. By day it is parked in the crystal city, at dusk it flies out through the tunnel at medium-fast speed to the pyramid desert and does its tic-tac darts all night, and at dawn it flies back the same way','The middle of the tunnel is kept clear of trees so the saucer never flies through anything']},\n"+"{v:'v1.0.112', d:'2026-11-02', notes:['Agartha has moved for new and reset worlds: its giant cave mouth is now cut into the ice wall straight behind Blackstone Castle at the north edge of the map, with a snow causeway over the sea from the castle to it','The tunnel runs straight on, out past the edge of the map, for 2000 blocks - the edge barrier, the freezing and the ocean do not reach inside it - and at the end is Agartha, the secret crystal city outside the map with its own sky, clouds and warm light','Nothing is dug under the mainland any more. Walk back out of the tunnel start to return to the ice wall','The Game structures list now points its Agartha entrance at the new mouth']},\n"+"{v:'v1.0.111', d:'2026-11-02', notes:['The new pig and sheep models now use the original Glencraft animations: every leg swing, head nods and grazing, and pigs lying down, rolling over and wiggling in the mud, with mud on their coats','New Game structures tab in the Builder Tool library (Test World): every structure in the game is listed - crofts, the hag hut, all three castles and their bridges, the pyramid, the sphinx, the shipwreck, the rocket base, the Agartha entrance, landmarks and every tree type','Press Open to jump to a structure in edit mode with a gold outline. Change it with blocks, or hold a block and press Paint all with held block to recolour the whole thing, then press Save. Every new world you make uses your edited version, and Reset puts the original back','Removed the automatic outlines around everything, the Upload world button and the Upload builds button. My builds library stays']},\n"+"{v:'v1.0.110', d:'2026-11-02', notes:['Sheep now walk properly: their legs swing in step with how fast they move, and when standing still they gently bob their heads or dip down to graze','The new sheep model only came with a standing animation, so the walk is now made by the game itself. Pigs keep their own walking animation']},\n"+"{v:'v1.0.109', d:'2026-11-02', notes:['New pig model: pigs now use a detailed textured 3D pig with its own walking animation, scaled to pig size and still small enough to load fast on phones','New sheep model: sheep now use a detailed textured 3D sheep with a walking animation. Coloured fleeces still tint each sheep, and shearing, wool and sandstorm floating work as before','Pigs and sheep behave exactly as before, including mud rolling, sounds, drops and health. Zombies and haggis keep their current models for now']},\n"+"{v:'v1.0.108', d:'2026-11-02', notes:['Y in the inventory now puts each item in the next free hotbar slot, so pressing Y on several items fills slots 1, 2, 3 without replacing any. An item already on the hotbar stays where it is, and only a full hotbar swaps with your selected slot', 'The inventory layout is back to how it was before v1.0.98, keeping the bottom tabs, LB and RB switching, the B exit hint and the snappy moves', 'The 3D character is gone from the pause menu', 'Every menu now fits the screen in portrait and landscape on phones and on desktop, scrolling where needed', 'Agartha tunnel fix - lochs and rivers above the tunnel can no longer leak water into it, the tunnel and cavern are sealed with stone wherever water touches them', 'Checked - old saves with the brooch and quaich convert to the new items correctly']}, {v:'v1.0.107', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['SPACE - the Highland Rocket Base stands beside one of the farmers crofts, with a launch pad, a gantry and a rocket you can fly', 'Board the rocket and the view goes third person. Hold THRUST (or Space) to lift off, steer with the move stick or WASD, EXIT once you have landed', 'No height limit for flight - climb past the build height through the atmosphere as the sky turns dark, through The Firmament, a shimmering layer high above, and out into deep space with stars', 'Mars - far out in space but the rocket is fast, about a minute away. In deep space the rocket steers for it by itself', 'Land on the red surface of Mars under its dusty pink sky, get out and walk in low gravity, then board again and fly up to head home to Earth', 'Light on phones - the base, the stars and Mars are only drawn when you need them, no world blocks are changed']}, {v:'v1.0.106', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Agartha v2: the giant entrance is now in the ice wall at the edge of the map, with a snowy landing in front of it', 'The tunnel is three times bigger and runs about 2000 blocks deep, with stone and grass walls and overgrown trees', 'Glowing blue grass and plants appear deeper in and grow thicker as you get close to Agartha', 'The Agartha cavern has about four times the air space, a blue sky with drifting clouds, a bigger inner sun and a bigger crystal city', 'No freezing and no barrier inside the cave', 'The brooch and quaich items moved to new ids, old saves are converted on load', 'Agartha v2 appears in new worlds and after Reset world, the old cave stays in old worlds']}, {v:'v1.0.105', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Real crystal blocks - cyan, violet and white crystals that glow on their own, now used for the Agartha crystal city (existing spires are converted)','Diamond and lazurite blocks are plain again - no more glow','A warm golden haze in Agartha','Old unused sounds, music and icons removed - the game download is about 23 MB smaller','Honeycomb and bottles keep working in old saves']},\n{v:'v1.0.104', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Agartha is bright and warm - the tunnel and the inner world never drop below the brightness floor, with a golden haze','The crystal city really glows - cyan diamond and violet lazurite crystal spires shine on their own, with white lantern crystals on the terraces. Diamond and lazurite blocks now glow softly everywhere','Ice is fully solid now, never see-through, so it costs no frame rate']},\n{v:'v1.0.103', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Smoother frame rate - far away chunks skip their grass, flowers and undergrowth, which the mist hides anyway, so far fewer things are drawn each frame','Close by everything looks exactly the same']},\n{v:'v1.0.102', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['AGARTHA - every new world hides one giant cave mouth. It slopes down into a huge winding tunnel about 2000 blocks long, packed with trees, moss, ferns, hanging leaves and glowing plants','At the end lies Agartha - a vast inner world with its own glowing central sun, warm mist and drifting sparkles, always lit','A crystal city of tall glowing spires with lamp crowns, terraces, crystal bridges and gardens','The Agarthans - very tall slender folk in light blue with bright blond hair and glowing blue eyes. Silent, peaceful and always there','Builder Tool - the Agartha tunnel, city and each crystal tower show up as pieces','Your saved worlds are not changed']},\n{v:'v1.0.101', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New worlds - a real coast all round the map: ragged shorelines, sandy beaches, then open sea getting deeper out to the ice wall, which now rises straight out of the ocean','The land gives up a little room at the edges for the sea - the world size is the same','Your saved worlds are not changed']},\n{v:'v1.0.100', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Pause menu - the D-pad now reaches the Help button too','Pause menu - your 3D character now shows on phones as well, smaller in landscape']},\n{v:'v1.0.99', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Crafting tabs - All, Construction, Nature and Items. Search looks through every recipe','Bag tabs - All plus one tab for each kind of item you carry','Armour slot names are readable again (two rows of three)','Pause menu - your 3D character turns beside the buttons, with small Patch notes and Help buttons underneath','Recipes you cannot make yet really show red now']},\n{v:'v1.0.98', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New menu layout in the Glencraft gold style','Inventory - your bag and hotbar column on the left, armour on the right with all slots in a row over your 3D character (RS turns it)','Inventory and Crafting tabs along the bottom - LB and RB switch, B exits','Crafting - a Search box, and a 3x3 grid that fills with the recipe, an arrow and the result. Things you cannot make yet are red','Pause - a clean stack of big buttons: Resume, Settings, Upload world and builds in Test World, Reset world, Save and quit','Show legs in first person now sits in Settings - Graphics']},\n{v:'v1.0.97', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Settings - Graphics - Show legs in first person (on by default)','Inventory - picking up and moving items is instant, only the slots that change are redrawn','Y in the bag always lands the item on the hotbar - if it is already there it swaps into your selected slot','RS turns your character in the inventory smoothly, at your controller look sensitivity','Armour and the jetpack go on with no lag spike - their looks are warmed up when the world loads','Crafting - recipes you cannot make yet are tinted red']},\n{v:'v1.0.96', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Builder Tool - no more corner marking. Everything the world makes near you is found by itself: houses, castles, bridges, landmarks, every tree, lava pools, caves and ravines, each with an outline and a label (nearest is green)','Test World starts you holding the Builder Tool. Blocks you change are tinted blue as part of that piece, then Save piece (on screen, RT or X with the tool, or G) stores it and Upload builds exports it','Saved trees become that tree type in new worlds','First person - the body view is gone. Look down and you see only your two legs walking with you, never in the way when looking ahead','Gun aiming and Builder Tool both stay off LT for blocks - LT still places blocks and trades']},\n{v:'v1.0.95', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Guns - hold LT to aim down the sights: the view zooms in, the gun comes to the middle and shots go dead straight. RT fires. Firing from the hip has a little spread','Without a gun LT still places blocks and trades as before','Builder Tool - corners are marked with RT (left click) now, so LT is free','First person - look down and you see your own legs, kilt and body walking and running with you','Smoother walking - leg and arm swings ease in and out in first and third person']},\n{v:'v1.0.94', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New Builder Tool in any world called test world - mark corner A and corner B (a gold box shows what is captured) and pick which build it replaces','Builds you can swap: croft houses, the hag hut, bridges over rivers and lochs, and landmarks scattered over the map','Pause - World - My builds library to view, delete or recapture your builds, and How to use Builder Tool for the steps','Pause - World - Upload builds saves builds_default.json - Send this file to Grok Bot - your builds go into everyones new worlds','New worlds stay random but use your builds - set on the ground with foundations filled, the space above cleared and turned the right way, bridges stretch to fit each gap','Castles, the pyramid and the volcano stay fixed for now because the quests and story live in them','New Packed snow block - solid white snow with a fine crunchy grain and a slight blue shade, now used for the ice wall and in the Bag of Everything','Smoother frame rate - the lazurite ore texture was being reloaded every frame by two old painters fighting each other','Your saved worlds are not changed']},\n{v:'v1.0.93', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Ice wall edge fixed - no more floating thin snow layers, the wall is solid snow blocks only','Every new world starts with a pistol and a musket, and both have infinite bullets','Caves now have natural gravel patches and veins, and a shovel digs gravel much faster','Lazurite ore now blends into the stone texture, and silver ore looks like real shiny silver','Lava pools at the bottom of the deep caves, and spiders are back in caves only','Water bug fixed - flowing water can no longer push you into a block, and if you ever get stuck inside one you are pushed out','Upload world now shows in the pause menu of any world called test world, however it is spelled','No more Random world option - new worlds start on the uploaded map when there is one','Repair world button removed','Desert sandstorms come and go now - long calm spells with the odd storm that blows in and fades away','Alien abduction fades out the game and desert music and plays the trippy alien music again, then the normal music comes back','YEAR 24000 fixed - it is now the real desert and pyramid around you turned solid shiny silver, no more see-through mess','After Upload world: Send this file to Grok Bot - it becomes the map for everyones new worlds']},\n{v:'v1.0.92', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Ice wall fixed - no more see-through ice, it is now solid icy snow blocks so there is no lag','The ice wall is about three times taller and stepped so you can climb it','Climb over the wall or wander off the edge of the map and you start freezing - frost on the screen, a warning and you slowly lose hearts until you head back inside','New desert music - your own track now plays around the pyramid desert and loops smoothly forever','Sandstorm fixed - no more blowing sand or haze inside the pyramid, caves or under a roof','Only new or reset worlds get the new wall, your saved worlds are not changed']},\n{v:'v1.0.91', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New Highlands map for new and reset worlds - one connected mainland with lochs, mountain rivers, hills and mountains, rounded corners and a huge ice wall around the edge','OG spawn - plain oak trees, grass, flowers and haggis round spawn, no dinosaurs near spawn and only one dinosaur in the world at a time','Tall pine forests, purple heather moors and juniper bushes with bluebells and ferns across the glens','Caves are different in every world, with fun cave mouths at the foot of mountains and far fewer random holes in the ground','Winding gravel paths from spawn to the castles, the desert and the volcano - they dig through hills in trenches and lamp-lit tunnels instead of going over them','The volcano is moved far away to the north-east mountains, and eruptions now have a huge ash column and cloud, a rolling ash surge, glowing embers, lightning and a camera shake - kept light for phones','Desert music only plays in the pyramid desert, not on every sand block','The UFO only comes at night over the pyramid desert','Grass, flowers and ferns look more solid and 3D with no black edges','Upload world (Test World only, in the pause menu) saves the map as world_default.json.gz - send it to Grok Bot to publish it, then every new world starts on that map','New World has a Random world option to ignore the published map','Menus - the selected button in the worlds list grows too, and the focus ring follows your UI colour','Your saved worlds are not changed']},\n{v:'v1.0.90', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New gold UI theme everywhere - dark buttons with a glowing gold border, gold serif button text and a carved gold GLENCRAFT logo','The selected button (controller, hover or touch) now smoothly grows and glows brighter so moving through menus feels like a scrolling selector','Settings - Graphics - UI colour: pick Gold, Neon green, Ice blue, Tartan red, Heather or Silver, or any custom colour - it recolours every menu and is saved']},\n{v:'v1.0.89', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Test World always starts now - if its save is missing or broken a fresh new world is made in the same slot, no prompt','Every new or reset world starts with the Bag of Everything along with the starter kit']},\n{v:'v1.0.88', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: a world reset no longer deletes the old save before the new world is ready - closing the game mid-reset can never leave a world with no save again','A world whose save went missing loads its newest backup if there is one, or offers Rebuild world','If a world fails to start or takes more than 15 seconds, a small box shows the error so you can screenshot it','New Repair button next to each world - clears stuck loading or reset state, never touches your blocks or items']},\n{v:'v1.0.87', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: older worlds start safely - the newer pyramid, painting and folk add-ons can no longer stop a world from loading, and if a world hits a snag the game tries its other saved copy instead of giving up. Your save is never wiped']},\n{v:'v1.0.86', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: the Egyptians no longer disappear - the pyramid is remembered with your world, missing folk come back at the pyramid, and any that wander off walk home']},\n{v:'v1.0.85', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Reset world: the Glencraft loading screen now comes up first, before anything changes, with a progress bar and percentage, and lifts once the new world is drawn','After a reset you land back where you were standing, on top of the new ground - your things are kept as before','The paintings in the pyramid gallery sit flat on the walls instead of poking into them','No more monsters spawning inside the pyramid - creepers and the rest stay out, the Egyptians stay']},\n{v:'v1.0.84', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: the stray phone notification sound is gone from the desert music','The desert music now plays on endlessly without an obvious repeat - it blends random parts of the tune together for as long as you stay']},\n{v:'v1.0.83', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New desert music made from your own clip, looping smoothly','Desert music no longer cuts out when you fly over the desert','The pyramid hall is longer and taller, with two new gallery rooms','Your own paintings now hang framed in the pyramid gallery rooms (new or reset worlds)','Dance music: no more loud noise at the end - the song loops cleanly','The dancers keep dancing while you stay near - walk away or press LT to stop']},\n{v:'v1.0.82', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: the UFO comes back at night - until you finish the encounter it now arrives early in your first night, anywhere, not only in the desert']},\n{v:'v1.0.81', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Dance music is now loud and clear - normalised and played on the music volume, with a much gentler distance fade','New calmer desert and temple music: Desert theme by yd (CC0)']},\n{v:'v1.0.80', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New: the Egyptian dance has new music - a track by Frankie Maxwell, looping for the whole dance. Your own Custom dance music in Settings still takes over if you pick one']},\n{v:'v1.0.79', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: in the desert the main background music now crossfades out as the desert temple tune comes in, and back again when you leave, so only one plays at a time']},\n{v:'v1.0.78', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New: new original desert dance music for the Egyptian dance - flute, oud and hand drums at the same tempo as the moves','New: a new original Egyptian temple tune plays in the desert and round the pyramid','New: Settings then Audio then Custom dance music - choose your own music file for the dance. It is kept only on this device and never uploaded. Use built-in switches back','Egyptians: dance moves redone to match the video, and the terrain music now fades out for the whole dance while the dance music plays from the group']},\n{v:'v1.0.77', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Egyptians: dance moves redone to match the video - clasp, arm bars, L-shapes, the diamond, hands on head, eye circles, the flute, face covers, open hands, paws and the double point','Fix: during the dance the terrain and desert music now fade out for the whole dance and come back after, and the dance music really plays in 3D from the group (it was silent before)','New: ready for your own music - put your dance track in as assets/music/dance_custom.mp3 and your Egyptian temple track as assets/music/temple_custom.mp3 and they play instead of the built-in tunes']},\n{v:'v1.0.76', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New: a Patch notes button on the main menu right under Play and Settings - controller friendly too','New: water really flows now - moving ripples that follow the river, foam on the crests and sky reflections (three.js water normals, MIT)','New: lava flows too - a glowing crust that slowly creeps along and pulses with heat (ambientCG Lava004, CC0)','New: a Bag of Everything in your inventory - hold it and use it to open a bag with one stack of every item and block in the game. Given once per world, take what you like and put things back']},\n{v:'v1.0.75', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: Reset world now hides behind the Glencraft loading screen - you see the glowing logo and Resetting world while the new glen is made, never a frozen game or the old land, and it lifts once the new world is ready and drawn']},\n{v:'v1.0.74', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: Reset world keeps everything you carry - inventory, armour and XP come with you to the new world. The starter kit only goes to brand-new worlds','New: the alien encounter is less than half as long (about 95 seconds) and every line is spoken only once','New: the alien now waits inside the crashed saucer until you walk within about 4 blocks of it','New: the vision clips play full screen and fully opaque, with three more public-domain NASA clips - an aurora from the ISS, a solar flare and a volcano erupting from orbit','Fix: the drawn bomb picture is gone from the visions','New: the chrome YEAR 24000 is back - every block, the pyramid, sand, statues and trees turn mirror chrome with a neon grid floor, a purple sky and saucers, built behind the last clip so it starts smoothly, and everything is restored after','Mobs: no mobs spawn and all mobs pause during the YEAR 24000 vision, then carry on as normal','New: the saucer crash crater fills with a flat, glowing pool of Element 115','Fix: the TV meteor warning now stays on screen for about 10 seconds','Egyptians: the Egyptians outside the pyramid stay together in one village group and never vanish when you walk away','Fix: the alien painting now hangs inside the chest room down the pyramid staircase, and only after the encounter','Fix: the old grass block is gone from the loading screen']},\n{v:'v1.0.73', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: LT on an Egyptian works again on controller and touch - it picks the nearest Egyptian within about 4 blocks in front of you, so you no longer need perfect aim','New: the LT dance chain is back in full - the Egyptians group up in rows, then dance the keyframed routine in sync with the music','New: YEAR 24000 turns every block mirror silver again on top of the original vision, and everything goes back to normal after','New: the meteor is back - after the encounter the TV says brace for impact, the alien voice repeats it with a deep roar and the meteor starts as a far speck and grows as it comes in','Mobs: the Timmer Tiki stays switched off','Fix: patch notes for v1.0.66 to v1.0.73 are all listed in Pause then Info then Patch notes']},\n{v:'v1.0.72', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: the alien encounter is back to the original version - the earlier voice, the earlier cool hallucinations and the original YEAR 24000, smooth with no lag','Story: the alien speaks for itself in first person - its own warnings about watching your skies, your weapons and what fell from the sky','Mobs: the Timmer Tiki that kept knocking is switched off - it no longer spawns or makes sounds and any already in your world are removed']},\n{v:'v1.0.71', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['Fix: the alien encounter, the YEAR 24000 vision and the meteor are back to the smooth v1.0.67 versions (no more lag), keeping only the safety timer so you can never stay frozen','Story: the alien now speaks for itself - its own warnings about watching your skies, your weapons and what fell, in the ethereal voice, with no names or captions','Fix: Reset world deletes the old save first, never shows a could not save error and builds the new map nearest first a few chunks at a time','Fix: Reset world is a full new world - new seed and fresh mobs, story, inventory, XP and position (settings are kept)','New: the big saucer only appears at night and flies off at dawn - a crashed wreck stays','Fix: the spinning grass block on the loading screen is no longer black','New: new and reset worlds start with a map, a diamond axe and an unlimited XP splash potion - throw it as often as you like for a shower of XP orbs','Fix: LT on an Egyptian only starts or stops the dance - it never places a block or uses your item','New: a glowing controller and Bluetooth badge in the bottom right of the main menu - it lights up when a controller is connected','Egyptians: the dance gathers everyone into neat rows first, then they all start in sync']},\n{v:'v1.0.70', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New: when you press LT on an Egyptian the nearby Egyptians first walk over and group up in neat rows facing you, stepping around blocks','New: once everyone is in place (or after about 6 seconds) they all start the dance on the same beat in perfect sync and the music starts with them','Fix: when the dance ends the Egyptians walk back to their stones, prayers, fields and drums']},\n{v:'v1.0.69', d:'2026-11-01', notes:['New: animal sounds are true 3D - every sheep, pig, duck and haggis call comes from where the animal stands, pans left and right as you turn and fades out by about 24 blocks','Fix: animal voices no longer pile up - one call per animal at a time and only a few at once','Mobs: pigs are a proper animated pig again (walk, idle, eat and run) wearing the real pig photo - the face and snout on the head and the pink wrinkled skin on the body','Mobs: pig hitbox, behaviour and mud rolling are unchanged','Audio: animal sounds are much quieter and the harsh sheep yell is gone - only gentle bleats','New: sound occlusion - sounds behind walls or heard from indoors are muffled and quieter','Fix: the alien abduction no longer freezes - the dialogue and music are back, the alien voice is ethereal with echo, chorus and airy reverb','Visual: YEAR 24000 vision is cleaner - no daylight sky, clouds or speech bubble showing through and the giant robots stand farther away','New: the meteor appears the moment the alien says brace for impact - a small far speck that grows as it comes in with a building roar into the impact','New: original Egyptian desert soundtrack crossfades in when you walk onto the sand and fades back out when you leave, UFO music takes over when it arrives','Fix: the alien painting only appears after the alien encounter and hangs flat on the hall wall','New: many more Egyptians around the pyramid - carrying stones, kneeling in prayer, farming with hoes and playing drums','New: aim at an Egyptian and press LT to start a synced meditation dance - every Egyptian nearby dances the same routine to an original 97 BPM arabesque track heard from the dancers, press LT again or walk away to stop']},\n",1)
